      "match_type": "bo5",
      "played_at": "2025-07-19T16:00:00Z",
      "notes": "What a match! Down 1-2 and came back to win it. Best match of the summer.\n\nThis was the kind of match that makes you love squash. Alice was playing incredible in games 2 and 3 — her drops were **unreadable** and she was covering the front like a wall.\n\nI told myself at 1-2 down: *just focus on length and width, make her play one more shot every rally*.\n\nGame 4 I played the most disciplined squash of my life. Every ball deep, every serve tight. Alice started to tire and I could see her shots getting looser.\n\nGame 5 was pure adrenaline. At 8-8 I hit a backhand nick that I'll remember forever. Closed it out 11-8.\n\n## Stats\n- Total rallies: ~180\n- Longest rally: 42 shots (game 3)\n- Unforced errors: way too many in games 2-3, almost none in 4-5",
